# ── OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# ── Private vault — never committed ──────────────────────────
brain/

# ── Read-only reference clones ───────────────────────────────
.references/*
!.references/README.md
!.references/references.toml

# ── Local snapshots ──────────────────────────────────────────
.snapshots/

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
# Key and certificate files are secrets and live in brain/ (AGENTS.md section
# 7); a build reads them from there. Ignored everywhere else, because a save
# takes every file git does not ignore: an Android .keystore next to the app
# was one save away from GitHub.
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.mobileprovision

# ── What the backbone's own tools leave behind ───────────────
# Every project carries upstream.py and radar.py, so every project can grow a
# __pycache__/ the moment `just upstream` runs. The scheduled run of 2026-09-22
# staged one: a save takes every file git does not ignore. A tracked .pyc is
# worse than clutter — it holds the source's mtime, so a fresh checkout
# recompiles it, `git status` is never empty again, and step 0 of the routine
# brief stops every later run before it starts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Code map — only the readable report is committed ─────────
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/README.md

# ── Agent local state ────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.gemini/
.aider*
.windsurf/

# ── Editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── YOUR STACK GOES HERE ─────────────────────────────────────
# Add your language's build artifacts below, or keep them in a
# stack-specific template. Examples:
#   Rust:   target/
#   Node:   node_modules/  dist/  .next/
#   Python: __pycache__/  .venv/
#   Swift:  *.xcodeproj  DerivedData/  .build/
#   Flutter: .kotlin/   and keep the .gitignore files `flutter create` writes
#           inside the app: they cover build/ and .dart_tool/ there, and not
#           at a pub workspace's root (stack-flutter.just names the lines).
#           Never *.xcodeproj here: ios/Runner.xcodeproj is part of the app.
